    "created_at": "2016-06-08T02:07:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-08T02:07:19Z",
    "body": "If we were to specify that these are supported as part of Fetch (in addition to navigation), and as a result, could be handled by service workers, I can think of at least a few use cases that wouldn't otherwise be possible:\n- Service worker protocol handlers - e.g: implement a SW that handles magnet: URIs and uses [feross/webtorrent](https://github.com/feross/webtorrent) to retrieve content, without the caller needing any understanding of BitTorrent specifics.\n-  Service worker content handlers - e.g: implement a SW that handles image/bpg and can transparently convert to image/png in browsers lacking native support.\n\nThere would, of course, need to be some thought & discussion around the security & permissions model for this\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
